From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] urlmon: Pump thread user messages during synchronous binds.

Embedded browser clients may schedule protocol work through a hidden window on
the binding thread.  The synchronous binding loop currently wakes for those
posted messages but only dispatches messages addressed to URLMon's private
notification window.  This leaves the browser's scheduler message queued until
the nested binding has timed out, causing resource requests and launcher window
creation to stall.

Keep the existing restricted user-message range, but remove the window filter
so all matching messages owned by the binding thread can make progress.  This
matches the thread-wide queue observed by MsgWaitForMultipleObjects() and does
not pump keyboard, mouse, paint, or other messages outside that range.
---
 dlls/urlmon/binding.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/urlmon/binding.c b/dlls/urlmon/binding.c
index 50d9910d68f3..77b700281e86 100644
--- a/dlls/urlmon/binding.c
+++ b/dlls/urlmon/binding.c
@@ -1598,7 +1598,7 @@ static HRESULT start_binding(IMoniker *mon, Binding *binding_ctx, IUri *uri, IBi
     while(!(binding->bindf & BINDF_ASYNCHRONOUS) &&
           !(binding->state & BINDING_STOPPED)) {
         MsgWaitForMultipleObjects(0, NULL, FALSE, 5000, QS_POSTMESSAGE);
-        while (PeekMessageW(&msg, binding->notif_hwnd, WM_USER, WM_USER+117, PM_REMOVE|PM_NOYIELD)) {
+        while (PeekMessageW(&msg, NULL, WM_USER, WM_USER+117, PM_REMOVE|PM_NOYIELD)) {
             TranslateMessage(&msg);
             DispatchMessageW(&msg);
         }
